  "description": "PEYTIA crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P 1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C104 H86 Eu2 N4 O26 Ti4. From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Ti1 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; Ti4 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; Ti2 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; Ti3 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.854-3.774 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.17-143.29°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Eu2Ti4(μ2-O)2(μ3-O)4(+pbpy)2(ba)10. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ2-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
